<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  SpotBugs exclude filter for the backend.

  The build reports only HIGH-priority findings (threshold=High in pom.xml), and the current code has none, so
  nothing is suppressed yet.

  Do not disable a whole bug category here. When a High finding is a genuine false positive (for example a
  Lombok-generated accessor), suppress that one case with <Match> on class + bug pattern (+ field or method) and
  state the reason in a comment placed above the entry, e.g.:

    Reason: why this specific case is safe.
    <Match>
      <Class name="com.page24.backend.entity.Example"/>
      <Bug pattern="EI_EXPOSE_REP"/>
      <Field name="items"/>
    </Match>

  Note: a comment must not contain two consecutive hyphens, and SpotBugs only logs (does not fail) when this file
  is unreadable, so check the build log for "Unable to read filter" after editing it.

  Known findings that appear only if the threshold is lowered to Medium (not reported today, 14 in total):
    EI_EXPOSE_REP / EI_EXPOSE_REP2 (7): CarePlanDownload.content, ReportFile.content (byte[] in records),
      PatientHasActiveOrdersException.activeOrderIds (List), LLMAdapterFactory.llmServices (Spring-injected)
    CT_CONSTRUCTOR_THROW (3): CreateOrderHandler, GenerateCarePlanHandler, IntakeAdapterFactory
    VA_FORMAT_STRING_USES_NEWLINE (3): ClaudeService, OpenAIService, DataInitializationService
    NP_BOOLEAN_RETURN_NULL (1): CreateOrderHandler
-->
<FindBugsFilter>
</FindBugsFilter>
